{"name":"Milky Way","hex":"#e8f4f7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Milky Way","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The Milky Way Galaxy, the galaxy in which Earth is located. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A broad band of diffuse white light, visible in the night sky; our view of the dense portions of the Milky Way Galaxy from inside the galaxy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Milky_Way"}],"entries":[{"title":"Milky Way","blocks":[{"text":"The Milky Way or Milky Way Galaxy, or simply the Galaxy, is the galaxy that includes the Solar System, with the name describing the galaxy's appearance from Earth: a hazy band of light seen in the night sky formed from stars in other arms of the galaxy, which are so far away that they cannot be individually distinguished by the naked eye."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/ESO-VLT-Laser-phot-33a-07.jpg/330px-ESO-VLT-Laser-phot-33a-07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milky_Way","wikidata":"Q321"},{"title":"Milky Way (chocolate bar)","blocks":[{"text":"Milky Way is an American brand of malt-flavored milk chocolate-covered confectionery snacks manufactured and marketed by Mars Inc. since 1923. Created by Frank Mars, it was his first chocolate bar product. There are two varieties of Milky Way: the original American bar made of nougat and caramel, which has been marketed as the Mars bar outside the United States; and the global Milky Way bar which has no caramel, and is marketed as 3 Musketeers in the U.S. and Canada."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Milky-Way-Bars-USUK-Whole.jpg/330px-Milky-Way-Bars-USUK-Whole.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milky_Way_(chocolate_bar)","wikidata":"Q1752705"},{"title":"Milky","blocks":[{"text":"Milky is an Italian dance music production group consisting of producers Giordano Trivellato and Giuliano Sacchetto, with Italian singer Giuditta Gazza serving as their lead singer on their album Star. They are best known for their 2002 single \"Just the Way You Are\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milky","wikidata":"Q6858151"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Milky_Way_Night_Sky_Black_Rock_Desert_Nevada.jpg/500px-Milky_Way_Night_Sky_Black_Rock_Desert_Nevada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Milky_Way_Night_Sky_Black_Rock_Desert_Nevada.jpg/1280px-Milky_Way_Night_Sky_Black_Rock_Desert_Nevada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Milky_Way_Night_Sky_Black_Rock_Desert_Nevada.jpg/500px-Milky_Way_Night_Sky_Black_Rock_Desert_Nevada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Milky Way as seen from a dark site with little light pollution","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMilky_Way_Night_Sky_Black_Rock_Desert_Nevada.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Herschel-Galaxy.png/500px-Herschel-Galaxy.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Herschel-Galaxy.png/500px-Herschel-Galaxy.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The shape of the Milky Way as deduced from star counts by William Herschel in 1785. The Solar System was assumed to be near the center.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHerschel-Galaxy.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Pic_iroberts1.jpg/500px-Pic_iroberts1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src